This code implements the Aosong DHT20 driver class as per the provided specifications. It uses the `adafruit_ads1x15` library for I2C communication and the `picamera2` library for camera functionality (not used in this example). The `paho-mqtt` library is also imported but not used in this example. The `gpiozero` library is used for button functionality (not used in this example). The code includes error handling for I2C bus failures, CRC errors, and other exceptions. The `begin()` method waits 0.5s after power-on and polls the status register until bit 7 becomes zero. The `get_temperature_and_humidity()` method enforces a minimum two-second interval between calls and retries up to five times with a 0.01s pause between retries. The `close()` method shuts down the underlying library, and the `__enter__` and `__exit__` methods support use as a context manager. The demonstration loop handles `KeyboardInterrupt` and `SystemExit` exceptions and exits with code 0 if `begin()` fails.

